From what I can tell by looking at the source, Excalibur always grants
automatic searching regardless of enchantment.  However, any positive
enchantment will, additionally, improve to the odds of finding secret
doors or passages (but not traps!), in exactly the same way as wearing
lenses does.

The exact condition for searching find a hidden door or passage is
rnl(7-fund) == 0, where fund is the enchantment of wielded Excalibur
(or otherwise 0), plus 2 if wearing lenses, capped at 5, and rnl() is
the infamous luck-adjusted random number generator.  The condition for
finding traps is always rnl(8) == 0.  Thus:

 * Enchanting Excalibur above +5 (or +3 if wearing lenses) will not
   further improve the odds of finding secret doors or passages.

 * If your luck is -3 or less, your chance of finding anything is less
   than 1% whether you have the +5 Excalibur or not.

 * If your luck is between -2 and 2, the odds of finding a secret door
   are much better, going from 14% at +0 to 50% at +5.

 * If your luck is maxed (13), either a +2 Excalibur or a pair of
   lenses is enough to guarantee a 98% success rate.

 * The chance of finding traps is _only_ affected by luck, going from
   12% at -2 to 2 up to 61% at 13, not by having Excalibur or lenses.

(Percentage values courtesy of the Nethack rnl() odds Calculator,
http://klozoff.ms11.net/cgi-bin/nethack-rnl-calculator.pl)

